 except for sinister  strange who really just wore it down  utilizing the same outfit from end game  designers added a lot of dark magic  effects to this alternate strange and  all that was needed at this point was  the talented cumberbatch's acting he  really wanted to push toward the darker  edge of this character without making  him just another cheesy villain  number 10. well who knew that young  people loved tik tok we weren't mad  about that especially when sochil gomez  gets benedict wong to join in on a few  dances these two were quite the content  duo behind the scenes busting moves with  wong's signature bluetooth speaker  although it looks like benedict will  have to stretch a little more for  tick-tock she tried to teach me some  moves but uh  i think i pulled the muscle number 11 it  looks like marvel was caught red-handed  on this one we really thought  cumberbatch was randomly waving his  hands around but our feeble minds were  surprised to learn that it's not that  simple and choreographer jay funk was  brought on to give the magic behind the  hand movements each spell is directly  related to each specific hand movement  definitely gotta hand it to jay on this  one nice work  number 12 this entry is brought to you  by tuning forks the only way to get  elizabeth olsen to enjoy flying around  the set she's no stranger to harnesses  and unlike many other mcu actors she  actually enjoys being up there and  thrashing around i really do enjoy it a  lot those so-called big metal tuning  forks gave her a comfy huggy feeling  even though to us that just looks like a  whole lot of dizzy  number 13. did you catch that strange  comic book reference we'll talk about  the illuminati a little later but that  suit he's wearing in that scene is  actually inspired by the suit from the  comic in which strange was a part of the  secret society sam loved this idea  taking good care of comic nostalgia but  not forcing it on the audience there's  not much to be said about 